{
  "_comment": [
    "Suggested permission rules for .claude/settings.local.json (OA-10).",
    "The assistant cannot write to settings.local.json itself — the harness refuses edits to its",
    "own permission file as self-modification, and an explicit grant from the owner does not lift",
    "that, which is the point of the guard. So this is a copy-paste source, not a live file.",
    "",
    "To apply: open .claude/settings.local.json and replace its 'allow' array with the one below,",
    "or run /permissions in Claude Code and add the entries there.",
    "",
    "Two things will still prompt regardless of what is in the allow list, because they are",
    "safety classifiers rather than permission rules:",
    "  1. Commands that would print or materialise a credential value.",
    "  2. Production database writes and production deploys.",
    "The second is partly deliberate here: .claude/settings.json has a hook that blocks",
    "`vercel --prod`. Leave it. Pushing to main triggers the production build through the Git",
    "integration, which is the reviewed path."
  ],
